# CAF Free Plugin (always)

Free is **v3.0.0**, entry `category-ajax-filter.php`, `CAF_BUILDER_TIER=free`.  
Free ≠ Pro clone. Sync is one-way allowlisted from Pro (see Pro `caf-hub-spoke.mdc`).

**WP.org:** always apply `caf-wporg-guidelines.mdc` (Guideline 5 trialware).

## Ownership

| Owns | Examples |
|---|---|
| **Pro → sync** | `react-builder/build/`, allowlisted Free Woo / Elementor / range-slider from `free-plugin/` |
| **Free (this tree)** | Free `admin/builder-functions.php` sanitizers, entry, readme, Free tier PHP, most admin |

## Source of truth for React

- Edit React in **Pro** `react-builder/src`, then `build:free` / `release:free`.
- NEVER treat Free `react-builder/src` or `build/` as durable source of truth.
- Pro-only features: stub/NullModule at birth in Pro (`caf-new-pro-feature.mdc` / `caf-free-code-policy.mdc`). Do not mass-strip without approval.

## NEVER (wrong-direction)

- Replace Free normalize/sanitizers with Pro’s thinner `builder-functions.php`.
- Delete `caf_sanitize_free_*` when “syncing from Pro.”
- Copy Pro Woo stack; Free uses `class-caf-free-woo.php` only.
- Hand-edit Free React for a permanent Free-only feature (use tier / Free PHP / Pro free-replacements).

## WHEN Free-only fix after WP.org release

1. Edit Free-owned files here.
2. If the file is on the Pro sync allowlist, also port into Pro `scripts/free-plugin/` before the next `release:free`.
3. If not on allowlist, Free-only edit is enough (do not copy to Pro wholesale).

## WHEN shared UI bug

Fix in Pro React → `build:free` / `release:free` — do not fork Free JS.
